<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56518" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέλλω</span></b> , poet. (exc. <i><span class="en">
			D.H.
			14.1
		</span></i> as etym. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κελτική</span>),
		= Prose <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀκέλλω</span>: fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέλσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					331
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				1057
			</span></i> (lyr.), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κελῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκελσα</span> (v.
				infr.):—<i>drive on</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>, always in phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆα κέλσαι</span>
			<i>run</i> a ship <i>to land, put</i> her <i>to shore</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆα μὲν αὐτοῦ κέλσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					10.511
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆα . . ἐκέλσαμεν ἐν ψαμάθοισιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.546
				</span></i>
			; <i>cause to land</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδρῶν ἡρώων στόλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.1090
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄργει κ. πόδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					139
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr.,
			of ships or seamen, <i>put to shore</i> or <i>into harbour</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κελσάσῃσι δὲ νηυσὶ καθείλομεν ἱστία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					9.149
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέλσαντες Σιμόεντος ἐπ᾽ ἀκτάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					696
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Eu.</u>
				10
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς Ἄργος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					331
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς γῆν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					804
				</span></i>
			: c.acc. loci, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέλσαι . . Ἄργους γαῖαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					15
				</span></i>
			 (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τροίας ἄστυ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					934
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				186
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ποτὶ τέρμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					140
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾷ κέλσω</span>; where
				<i>shall I find a haven</i>? <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				1057
			</span></i> (lyr.). (Cf.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέλομαι</span>.)</div>
